Backend Specification Document: UGETJOB — Global Workforce Solutions (Nouman’s Manpower Consultancy)

Project context:
- This frontend is a static HTML/Tailwind landing page plus a job portal/admin ATS UI.
- The repo currently contains a single frontend page (`public/ugetjob.html`) with view switching between:
  - Landing page / marketing site
  - Jobs portal
  - Admin ATS portal
- The backend must support:
  - public job listing/search
  - candidate quick apply + resume upload
  - employer manpower inquiry submissions
  - service requests (recruitment / visa / documentation / mobilization)
  - admin ATS workflow for candidates

Important note:
- There are no actual frontend fetch calls in the repo as presented, so the API contract below is reverse-engineered from:
  - UI sections
  - modal forms
  - visible status values
  - job search/filter intent
  - ATS job workflow labels
- This is the clean contract a backend should implement.

1. Database Schema Requirements

1.1 Core design principle
Use PostgreSQL in Supabase with:
- UUID primary keys
- timestamptz for timestamps
- enum types for statuses
- foreign keys for relations
- JSONB for flexible metadata where needed
- storage bucket for resume and document files

1.2 Table list
- job_categories
- jobs
- candidates
- applications
- employers
- employer_inquiries
- service_requests
- application_documents
- job_search_activity (optional but useful)
- ats_notes (optional but useful)
- admin_users (optional)
- audit_logs (optional)

1.3 Table definitions

Table: job_categories
Purpose: controlled categories / sectors / industries for job search and filters

SQL:
```sql
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS job_categories (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    slug TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,
    name TEXT NOT NULL,
    description TEXT,
    parent_category_id UUID NULL REFERENCES job_categories(id),
    is_active BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT true,
    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),
    updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW()
);
```

Typical values:
- engineering
- construction
- electrician
- nurse
- healthcare
- hospitality
- oil-and-gas
- logistics
- security
- driver
- technician
- admin
- others

Table: jobs
Purpose: live job listings shown to candidates and admin ATS

SQL:
```sql
CREATE TYPE job_status AS ENUM ('draft', 'published', 'paused', 'closed', 'filled');

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS jobs (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    category_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES job_categories(id),
    title TEXT NOT NULL,
    company_name TEXT NOT NULL,
    employer_contact_name TEXT,
    employer_email TEXT,
    employer_phone TEXT,
    location_country TEXT NOT NULL,
    location_city TEXT,
    work_location_type TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'overseas', -- overseas, domestic, hybrid, remote
    visa_required BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT false,
    visa_type TEXT,
    employment_type TEXT NOT NULL, -- full_time, contract, temporary, project_based
    experience_min INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,
    experience_max INTEGER,
    age_min INTEGER,
    age_max INTEGER,
    gender_preference TEXT,
    nationality_preference TEXT,
    salary_min NUMERIC(12,2),
    salary_max NUMERIC(12,2),
    salary_currency TEXT DEFAULT 'INR',
    job_description TEXT NOT NULL,
    requirements TEXT,
    benefits TEXT,
    urgent BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT false,
    featured BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT false,
    skills TEXT[],
    openings_count INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1,
    deadline TIMESTAMPTZ,
    posted_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),
    expires_at TIMESTAMPTZ,
    status job_status NOT NULL DEFAULT 'published',
    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),
    updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW()
);
```

